  "modelingNotes": [
    "Vortex, Carowinds: procedural, CC0-1.0. bun generators/carowinds-vortex.ts (REPORT=1 for the element table)",
    "Built with ./coaster-kit.ts. Map frame: x east, y north, z up, metres; bearing 0. The origin is the middle of the track's footprint (ANCHOR), at the lowest ground under it.",
    "Plan: the chain of OSM roller_coaster=track ways from the west end of the station (way/669164155), all oneway, in the direction of travel: way/669205939, 894782920, 894782923, 894782917, 894782358, 894782912, 894782914, 894782918, 894782924, 894782925, 894782922, 894782919, 894782916, 894782915, 894782921, 894782913, 888642929 (609 m round).",
    "Profile: a B&M stand-up of 622 m (RCDB 86, Wikipedia, Coasterpedia): a 90 ft chain lift and pre-drop, the 80 ft curved drop to the right, a vertical loop, a rising right turn and a drop into a left upward helix, a smaller drop and a corkscrew to the right, a figure-eight turn, and a left turn into the brakes.",
    "Photos matched (Wikimedia Commons): \"Vortex (Carowinds) 2023 1\", Jeremy Thompson, CC BY 2.0 (from the Skytower; loop top measured at about 22 m); \"Vortex's red vertical loop and black supports from the path\", ThrillZing, October 2024, CC BY 4.0; \"Carowinds 023 (3145061684)\", Jeremy Thompson, CC BY 2.0 (helix and figure eight). Colours from the 2024 photos: red track, black supports since the 2023 refurbishment.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"carowinds-vortex\", model \"carowinds-vortex\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/carowinds-vortex.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches."
  ],
